  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "TanMinati loves solving problems.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of size NNN, where AiA_iAi​ represents the number of problems TanMinati solved on the iii-th day.\n\nA \"streak\" is defined as a sequence of consecutive days where TanMinati solves **at least 111 problem** every day.\n\nFind the length of the **longest streak** present among these NNN days.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the size of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,…,ANA_1, \\ldots, A_NA1​,…,AN​, where AiA_iAi​ denotes the number of problems solved by TanMinati on iii-th day.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the length of the longest streak by TanMinati.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100",
      "0≤Ai≤1000 \\leq A_i \\leq 1000≤Ai​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1\n1\n2\n5 0\n4\n0 5 2 0\n2\n0 0",
        "output": "1\n1\n2\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: TanMinati codes for only 111 day which is the longest streak.\nTest case 222: TanMinati coded on day 111 and rested on day 222 so the longest streak of TanMinati coding is 111 day.\nTest case 333: TanMinati coded on both days 222 and 333, so the longest streak of TanMinati coding is 222 days."
      }
    ]
  },
